{
  "_comment": [
    "DECISIVE TEST for the ~74 mm vertical: identical to _usgs_n141_m141.json except the",
    "two position_ecef entries are the published MARK (monument) coordinates rather than",
    "the ARP-reduced ones.",
    "PREDICTIONS, which are opposite:",
    "  H1 face-value (what ApplicationBaseline.cpp:173 appears to do): the reported VECTOR",
    "     is unchanged to <1 mm, because the data constrains antenna-to-antenna and a shift",
    "     in the held base cancels out (2 m of base error moves a 1352 m vector by 0.14 mm).",
    "  H2 delta applied internally somewhere: the vector's Up shifts by ~+75 mm, landing on",
    "     the ARP-to-ARP truth of 21.3394 -- proving -73.5 mm was bookkeeping, not physics.",
    "Solved Up with ARP coords was 21.2659, which is 1.5 mm from the antenna delta applied",
    "TWICE (21.2644).  That coincidence is what this test is chasing."
  ],
